[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6074627066","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124313#issuecomment-6074627066","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124313","id":6074627066,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABahNz-g","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-09T05:01:57Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T05:01:57Z","body":"I'm a little bit skeptical about this fix. It is almost always wrong to apply a fix to the core that was caused by a change outside of core. This is why our [best practices](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/best_practices.html#prefer-local-solutions) doc insists that contributors \"prefer local solutions\". If the regression was introduced in a particular system, the fix should likely live in that system as well. \r\n\r\nThe trouble with trying to patch something in core is you create knock-on effects that can impact performance or introduce bugs in other areas of the codebase that you haven't considered. \r\n\r\nThat isn't to say that this code is incorrect, but I suspect that it would be better to fix this in the physics MT wrapper instead","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6074627066/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6076985499","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124313#issuecomment-6076985499","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124313","id":6076985499,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABajdwmw","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-09T08:04:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T08:04:34Z","body":"Worth noting that `thread_local` has a cost, so if this is considered at all, it needs a performance test.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6076985499/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6080942619","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124313#issuecomment-6080942619","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124313","id":6080942619,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABanPSGw","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-09T12:31:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T12:32:12Z","body":"I had missed #123654 completely. I'll see if I can find some time to look into this in the next week or two.\r\n\r\n> Because _integrate_forces executes directly on the background physics thread\r\n\r\nThis isn't correct. `_integrate_forces` is (and always has been) called on the main thread.\r\n\r\nFrankly, I don't understand (without having stepped through the MRP) how there can be a recursive/re-entrant flush happening here to begin with, but if there is, then I assume this will be related to #113802 more so than #117268, since that's largely the code that's being changed here.\r\n\r\nJust quickly running the MRP in #123654 through a ThreadSanitizer build (`use_tsan=yes`) that's built from 3ea0cf3e72699c5e3b35f7956670ac93b9d1d4a0 yields no errors whatsoever for me, for the entire 50k frame run, which is even weirder.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6080942619/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]